<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13010" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dēmētrĭas</span></b> ,
			ădis, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημητριάς</span>, <i>a city in Thessaly</i>
			(Pelasgiotis), <i>newly colonized by Demetrius
				Poliorcetes</i>, formerly called Pagasae, now <i>Volo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 8, 15, § 29</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				27, 23 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">28, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">39, 23</span></i>.—
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dēmētrĭacus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>of Demetrias</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			 (al. Demetraicus).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A sort of plant</i>, Ap. Herb. 3.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
